-- Dogri in the server curriculum (generated by tools/gen_dogri_curriculum.py from tools/dogri_curriculum_data.py and Jammu & Kashmir's Dogri
-- First Week pack, frontend/content.js LANGUAGE_PACKS.jk.doi; data only). Dogri joins the CEFR catalogue at A1, with its review
-- record: a DRAFT with an AI-assisted pass, native-speaker review pending (docs/CONTENT_REVIEW.md). 9 lessons (the 7 First Week lessons, numbers
-- and money, help and health): their phrases (and the feminine form of the gendered one), 2 words each with an example, 3 grammar notes and 27
-- exercises (what a phrase means, translate it in Roman letters or Devanagari, fill in a word). 8 situations and a listening pair for every
-- lesson; browsers have no Dogri voice, so listening shows a labelled transcript. Corrections go in a new migration.
SELECT id, 'ai_assisted_review', 'pending', '2026-10-19',
       'A DRAFT written by the LingoBuddy team with an AI-assisted pass, with lower confidence than Hindi or Urdu; not yet checked by a native '
       || 'Dogri speaker, who should check every phrase. Masculine forms are taught first; the feminine form is shown where it differs. Browsers '
       || 'have no Dogri voice. Fares and practical tips change over time.'
FROM languages WHERE code = 'doi';

